---
import { example } from '../example.mjs';
import { presets, freshState, mappings, snapshot } from './model.mjs';
import { viewMatrix, svgMatrix, translation } from '../geometry.mjs';
import { groupMatrix } from './model.mjs';
const initial = freshState();
const fixed = presets.map(p => ({ p, result: snapshot(p), wrong: snapshot(p,'Card',true) }));
---
<figure class="gesture-comparison" data-gesture-comparison aria-labelledby="gesture-caption">
  <figcaption id="gesture-caption"><strong>Gesture comparison.</strong> Follow Review’s marked grab through one move, then try the same geometry in the live editor. Recorded traces are mathematical snapshots with the example’s client origin (120, 80). The live SVG uses this page’s current layout; its client coordinates will differ.</figcaption>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Starting state <select data-preset>{presets.map(p=><option value={p.id}>{p.label}</option>)}</select></label>
    <button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button>
  </div>
  <h3>Predict one move</h3>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Move <select data-trace-mode><option>Card</option><option>Pan</option></select></label>
    <label>Card update <select data-algorithm><option value="correct">Derived update</option><option value="wrong">Divide client movement by zoom</option></select></label>
    <label data-stale-wrap hidden><input type="checkbox" data-stale /> Use stale mapping after resize</label>
  </div>
  <p data-trace-start>Baseline: card translation G (30, 20), pan V (60, 40), zoom 2, view angle 0°. Pointer C (440, 400) → (480, 420).</p>
  <p class="legend">○ Grab before update · + Pointer target · ● Grab after update · outlined shape: Review after update. All positions below are in C.</p>
  <svg data-trace viewBox="180 110 380 390" role="img" aria-label="Client-space trace of the grab and pointer target">
    <line data-move-line x1="440" y1="400" x2="480" y2="420" class="motion" />
    <polygon data-result-card points="" class="result-card" />
    <g data-start-mark transform="translate(440 400)"><circle r="7" class="start-mark" /></g>
    <g data-pointer-mark transform="translate(480 420)"><path d="M-12 0H12M0-12V12" class="pointer-mark" /></g>
    <g data-result-mark><circle r="5" class="result-mark" /></g>
  </svg>
  <div data-arrows class="displacements" aria-label="The same pointer displacement in four spaces"></div>
  <button type="button" data-reveal>Reveal result</button>
  <p data-trace-result aria-live="polite">Predict where the grab will land, then reveal the result.</p>
  <p class="boundary">The arrows convert a movement using the current bridge. In the resize preset, movement alone cannot describe the change: the bridge also changed after the grab. Pan always uses the derived update; the two deliberate errors apply only where labelled.</p>

  <h3>Try the retained point</h3>
  <p>Choose <strong>Card</strong> and grab anywhere inside Review, or choose <strong>Pan</strong> and drag the board. Choose <strong>Choose pivot</strong> and press on the drawing to place the cross; the zoom and angle controls keep that V target. The centre is used until you choose one. <strong>Marked point as pivot</strong> provides a keyboard alternative.</p>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Tool <select data-tool><option>Card</option><option>Pan</option><option value="Pivot">Choose pivot</option></select></label>
    <button type="button" data-mark-pivot>Marked point as pivot</button>
    <button type="button" data-size>Toggle editor size</button>
  </div>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Zoom <input data-zoom type="number" min="0.25" max="4" step="0.25" value="2" /></label>
    <button type="button" data-zoom-more>Zoom × 1.5</button>
    <label>View angle (degrees) <input data-angle type="number" step="15" value="0" /></label>
    <label>Anchor rule <select data-anchor-rule><option value="correct">Keep chosen point</option><option value="pan">Keep old pan (wrong)</option><option value="angle">Ignore view angle (wrong)</option></select></label>
  </div>
  <p data-state class="state">Card translation G (30, 20) · zoom 2 · angle 0° · pan V (60, 40) · target V (400, 300)</p>
  <div class="editor-wrap">
    <svg data-editor viewBox="0 0 800 600" aria-label="Interactive Review board. Use the tool control to drag Card, Pan, or choose a pivot." role="img">
      <g data-world transform={svgMatrix(viewMatrix(initial.view))}>
        <path d="M0 0H350M0 0V250" class="world-axes" />
        <text x="5" y="-5" class="world-label">World W</text>
        <g data-group transform={svgMatrix(groupMatrix())}>
          <rect width={example.group.width} height={example.group.height} class="group-frame" />
          <path d="M0 0H35M0 0V35" class="group-axes" />
          <text x="4" y="-5" class="group-label">Review lane G</text>
          <g data-card transform={svgMatrix(translation(initial.card.x,initial.card.y))}>
            <rect width={example.card.width} height={example.card.height} class="review-card" />
            <text x="25" y="26" class="card-label">Review</text>
            <circle cx={example.p.x} cy={example.p.y} r="3" class="grab-mark" />
          </g>
        </g>
      </g>
      <g data-anchor-trace style="visibility:hidden">
        <g data-anchor-before><circle r="9" class="start-mark" /><text x="16" y="20">Anchor before</text></g>
        <g data-anchor-after><circle r="5" class="result-mark" /><text x="16" y="36">Anchor after</text></g>
      </g>
      <g data-target transform="translate(400 300)"><path d="M-12 0H12M0-12V12" class="pointer-mark" /><text x="16" y="-12">Target V</text></g>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <p data-anchor-summary aria-live="polite">Change zoom or angle to compare the anchor before and after.</p>
  <p class="boundary">The editor reserves touch gestures inside this surface with <code>touch-action: none</code>. The page around it keeps its normal scrolling. No wheel handling, multi-touch, inertia or undo is included. View changes and SVG attributes are committed together, with no independent CSS animation.</p>
  <p data-status class="state" aria-live="polite">Ready. No pointer event has been observed yet.</p>
  <details><summary>Read this figure as text</summary>
    <p>Each independent snapshot starts with Review at G (30, 20). The filled grab stays at O (10, 10). The derived card update reaches the pointer in every row.</p>
    <div class="outcomes">{fixed.map(({p,result,wrong})=><section><h4>{p.label}</h4><dl><dt>Pointer C</dt><dd>{`(${result.fromC.x}, ${result.fromC.y}) → (${result.targetC.x}, ${result.targetC.y})`}</dd><dt>Derived translation G</dt><dd>{`(${result.next.card.x}, ${result.next.card.y})`}</dd><dt>Divide-by-zoom grab C</dt><dd>{`(${wrong.landedC.x}, ${wrong.landedC.y})`}</dd></dl></section>)}</div>
    <p>For the turned, half-size pan, the pointer moves C (40, 20), V (80, 40), W (20, −40) and G (−40, −20). Pan becomes V (740, 0); card dragging instead makes the card translation G (−10, 0). Zoom 2 to 3 about the baseline mark keeps V (320, 320) by changing pan to (−70, −100). In the turned view it keeps V (380, 220) with pan (800, −170). Turning the baseline view 90° about the mark requires pan (600, 60).</p>
    <p>After resize between events, the current mapping gives card translation G (50, −20) and grab C (320, 260). A cached full-size inverse gives G (−40, 80) and grab C (220, 170).</p>
  </details>
</figure>
<script>
  import { mount } from './runtime.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-gesture-comparison]').forEach(mount);
</script>
<style>
  .gesture-comparison{margin:2rem 0;padding:1.1rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);color:var(--color-text);font-family:var(--font-sans);min-width:0;}
  figcaption{font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.6;}
  h3{font-size:1.1rem;margin:1.6rem 0 .6rem;}
  .controls{display:flex;gap:.65rem;align-items:end;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1rem 0;}
  label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.3rem;font-size:.82rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;}
  label:has(input[type="checkbox"]){flex-direction:row;align-items:center;}
  select,input,button{font:inherit;color:var(--color-text);background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-radius:.25rem;padding:.5rem;max-width:100%;}
  input[type="number"]{width:7rem;}button{font-size:.85rem;cursor:pointer;min-height:2.5rem;}
  :is(button,input,select):focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px;}
  p{font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.6;} .legend,.boundary{color:var(--color-text-secondary);font-size:.8rem;}
  [data-trace]{display:block;width:100%;height:22rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);}
  .motion{stroke:var(--color-text-secondary);stroke-width:2;stroke-dasharray:5 5;}
  .result-card{fill:var(--color-surface-alt);stroke:var(--color-accent);stroke-width:3;}
  .start-mark{fill:var(--color-surface);stroke:var(--color-text);stroke-width:2;}
  .result-mark{fill:var(--color-accent);}
  .pointer-mark{stroke:var(--color-text);stroke-width:2;fill:none;vector-effect:non-scaling-stroke;}
  .displacements{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.5rem;margin:.8rem 0;font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);}
  .displacements :global(svg){display:block;width:100%;height:4rem;}
  .displacements :global(path){stroke:var(--color-text);fill:none;stroke-width:2;}
  .state{font:.8rem/1.7 var(--font-mono);overflow-wrap:anywhere;}
  .editor-wrap{overflow:hidden;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);}
  [data-editor]{display:block;width:100%;max-width:800px;height:auto;touch-action:none;user-select:none;}
  [data-editor].half{width:50%;}
  .review-card{fill:var(--color-surface-alt);stroke:var(--color-accent);stroke-width:1.5;}
  .card-label,.group-label,.world-label,[data-target] text,[data-anchor-trace] text{fill:var(--color-text);font:11px var(--font-sans);}
  .group-frame{fill:none;stroke:var(--color-text-secondary);stroke-dasharray:4 3;}
  .world-axes,.group-axes{stroke:var(--color-text-secondary);fill:none;stroke-width:1;}
  .grab-mark{fill:var(--color-accent);}
  .outcomes{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;}
  h4{font-size:.9rem;}dl{font:.8rem/1.5 var(--font-mono);}dt{font-weight:bold;}dd{margin:0 0 .7rem;}
  summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:.9rem;}
  @media(max-width:600px){.gesture-comparison{padding:.75rem;} .controls{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr);}.controls :is(label,button,select){width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;} .displacements{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;} .outcomes{grid-template-columns:1fr;}[data-trace]{height:20rem;}}
</style>
